#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083042 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "385b1ccd-ea68-5c59-a0e6-1a0bb7937460" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations With Leading Coefficients by Grouping"}] :question/id #uuid "edbd084f-e8ad-53e7-9384-94094a6e7bc6" :question/math-academy-id "e-5879" :question/problem "Solve $2x^3+3x^2-8x-12=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-8x-12 & = \\\\ (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})-(8x+12) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(2x+3)-4(2x+3) & = \\\\ (2x+3)\\cdot {x}^{2}-(2x+3)\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ (2x+3)({x}^{2}-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(2x+3)(x^2-4) = 0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2x+3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-2, \\; -\\dfrac{3}{2}, \\; 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083043 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6158975-c81e-5621-aa39-3f2dc728f107" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Manipulating the Equation and Then Grouping"}] :question/id #uuid "90296377-6785-5b6d-87ca-8a88d4b266c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-5880" :question/problem "Solve $8x^3+3=4x^2+6x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we subtract $4x^2$ and $6x$ from both sides to make the right side $0.$ To prepare for factoring by grouping, we make sure to write the resulting cubic in standard form.\n\n$$\n8x^3-4x^2-6x+3=0\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6x+3 & = \\\\ (8{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2})-(6x-3) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{2}(2x-1)-3(2x-1) & = \\\\ (2x-1)\\cdot 4{x}^{2}-(2x-1)\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ (2x-1)(4{x}^{2}-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve.\n\n- Setting the factor $(2x-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-1 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(4x^2-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-3 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}, \\; \\dfrac12, \\; \\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083067 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7b17a61-b225-5493-98b0-58d15217aa31" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping"}] :question/id #uuid "1c104a42-2eea-5029-8ada-7d3bb90add52" :question/math-academy-id "e-6110" :question/problem "Solve $x^3+x^2-9x-9=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-9x-9 & = \\\\ ({x}^{3}+{x}^{2})-(9x+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+1)-9(x+1) & = \\\\ (x+1)\\cdot {x}^{2}-(x+1)\\cdot 9 & = \\\\ (x+1)({x}^{2}-9) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x+1)(x^2-9) = 0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x+1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =0 \\\\ x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-1, \\, \\pm  3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083068 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01d58dfd-315a-5a4f-ae16-1db04010169a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations With Negative Leading Coefficients by Grouping"}] :question/id #uuid "9d7a8d1c-449e-5e58-971f-7a063d52a703" :question/math-academy-id "e-6111" :question/problem "Solve $-x^3-4x^2+5x+20=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\nx^3+4x^2-5x-20=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x-20 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+4)-5(x+4) & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-5)(x+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x^2-5)(x+4)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x+4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-4, \\pm \\sqrt 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7b17a61-b225-5493-98b0-58d15217aa31" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b2afd65-6421-5c85-809b-f3d3bbc23063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 5,\\pm \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520133} {:answer/id #uuid "7804cb00-dc3d-59ca-985c-d750e65bdcfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5,-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520165} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f3d448-e53c-5baf-a19e-86cd0118bed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520262} {:answer/id #uuid "e32bec55-bb10-5bc2-9fe9-c78513ac1c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520321} {:answer/id #uuid "f13bd088-a5c4-52b8-8763-a1805c6f88af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f13bd088-a5c4-52b8-8763-a1805c6f88af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520346} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d8ec166-959b-5586-85f7-387a034ebd24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a147b6b-b927-5c0b-b768-701655ad01fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-114119" :question/problem "Find all of the real solutions to the equation ${x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+3x-15=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+3x-15 & = \\\\ ({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2})+(3x-15) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(x-5)+3(x-5) & = \\\\ (x-5)\\cdot {x}^{2}+(x-5)\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ (x-5)({x}^{2}+3) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x-5)({x}^{2}+3)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x-5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5 & =0 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({x}^{2}+3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+3) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince a squared real number cannot be negative, the equation ${x}^{2}+3=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore,  $x=5$ is the only real solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7b17a61-b225-5493-98b0-58d15217aa31" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0253d148-6cfe-5c62-a23b-66b9dbd84f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m=2,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519998} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4ed9a6-0960-541a-a947-eae413b4c345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m=\\sqrt{2},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520062} {:answer/id #uuid "510e6b93-921f-54a3-aaf4-f17810afc277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m=-3,\\,\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520114} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b976e5-3d11-5eb8-b26a-10408be52ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m=\\sqrt{3},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520295} {:answer/id #uuid "de8f6f1e-2d9f-5d34-897a-08a567c8845d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m=3,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de8f6f1e-2d9f-5d34-897a-08a567c8845d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m=3,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520313} :answer-field/id #uuid "93fde94e-983d-5d42-9eeb-795ef8488a6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "978fe695-4870-5063-84c2-77d196d63866" :question/math-academy-id "q-114145" :question/problem "Solve ${m}^{3}-3{m}^{2}-2m+6=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{3}-3{m}^{2}-2m+6 & = \\\\ ({m}^{3}-3{m}^{2})-(2m-6) & = \\\\ {m}^{2}(m-3)-2(m-3) & = \\\\ (m-3)\\cdot {m}^{2}-(m-3)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (m-3)({m}^{2}-2) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(m-3)({m}^{2}-2)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(m-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m-3 & =0 \\\\ m & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({m}^{2}-2)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ {m}^{2} & =2 \\\\ m & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=3,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7b17a61-b225-5493-98b0-58d15217aa31" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3add8b77-2674-550c-8c5e-937aa20f6757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-3,\\,\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520074} {:answer/id #uuid "6eaa3045-538f-5532-93c9-eb9d97b92258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-4,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520154} {:answer/id #uuid "76ad3e93-1d3d-503f-8bae-2aba16bc094a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-4,\\,\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520163} {:answer/id #uuid "7af9e36f-385d-53ce-95da-8a882f9bdffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=3,\\,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520169} {:answer/id #uuid "e11cb217-db6f-574c-b615-bccc13fddfb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=3,\\,\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76ad3e93-1d3d-503f-8bae-2aba16bc094a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-4,\\,\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520163} :answer-field/id #uuid "13e7c99c-7aef-53e8-bc54-39657119aa8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34ca4779-2bf7-5602-9812-9d6d9723327c" :question/math-academy-id "q-114146" :question/problem "Solve ${n}^{3}+4{n}^{2}-9n-36=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{3}+4{n}^{2}-9n-36 & = \\\\ ({n}^{3}+4{n}^{2})-(9n+36) & = \\\\ {n}^{2}(n+4)-9(n+4) & = \\\\ (n+4)\\cdot {n}^{2}-(n+4)\\cdot 9 & = \\\\ (n+4)({n}^{2}-9) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(n+4)({n}^{2}-9)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(n+4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n+4 & =0 \\\\ n & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({n}^{2}-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =9 \\\\ n & =\\pm 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $n=-4,\\,\\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "385b1ccd-ea68-5c59-a0e6-1a0bb7937460" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations With Leading Coefficients by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e895a8-20d5-5be3-91e6-fea5ef55ae13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520000} {:answer/id #uuid "556dab46-acc8-5752-9b58-7065d4927d67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d=\\pm \\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520123} {:answer/id #uuid "b5bc49b7-a136-5f0a-ba95-6eeee343a589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}},\\,\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520246} {:answer/id #uuid "f970778b-b4ef-590e-9c25-ab9706ce2474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d=\\pm \\frac{4}{9},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520355} {:answer/id #uuid "fa362661-1528-514a-98ce-2bf9cde68db6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d=\\pm \\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa362661-1528-514a-98ce-2bf9cde68db6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d=\\pm \\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520357} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd3ee59c-b21b-5bdc-b880-b22cc5016b54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bb562da5-ef3b-592a-bfc0-4d26f88b1f50" :question/math-academy-id "q-114198" :question/problem "Solve $36{d}^{3}-81{d}^{2}-16d+36=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36{d}^{3}-81{d}^{2}-16d+36 & = \\\\ (36{d}^{3}-81{d}^{2})-(16d-36) & = \\\\ 9{d}^{2}(4d-9)-4(4d-9) & = \\\\ (4d-9)\\cdot 9{d}^{2}-(4d-9)\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ (4d-9)(9{d}^{2}-4) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(4d-9)(9{d}^{2}-4)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(4d-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4d-9 & =0 \\\\ 4d & =9 \\\\ d & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(9{d}^{2}-4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{d}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ 9{d}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ d & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $d=\\frac{9}{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{2}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01d58dfd-315a-5a4f-ae16-1db04010169a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations With Negative Leading Coefficients by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35e4f392-48f5-541b-aa88-739a0fba7056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520071} {:answer/id #uuid "b98f9771-5de9-571d-96fe-04304b611ff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=6,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520250} {:answer/id #uuid "bc94728e-0409-57f5-a0a4-2df3910b17c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=6,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520255} {:answer/id #uuid "dcb2caea-0ad4-571d-987f-a03f34b6b81d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=6,\\,\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520309} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa87e20-7120-5b08-8f33-95132a4dcbe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=2,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b98f9771-5de9-571d-96fe-04304b611ff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=6,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520250} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd45dfb-9cad-5c3d-946b-21eb406e1d7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bbddec8f-0415-5a7f-a473-3ac96a89f653" :question/math-academy-id "q-114207" :question/problem "Solve $-2{r}^{3}+12{r}^{2}+3r-18=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\n2{r}^{3}-12{r}^{2}-3r+18=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{r}^{3}-12{r}^{2}-3r+18 & = \\\\ (2{r}^{3}-12{r}^{2})+(-3r+18) & = \\\\ 2{r}^{2}(r-6)-3(r-6) & = \\\\ (2{r}^{2}-3)(r-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(2{r}^{2}-3)(r-6)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2{r}^{2}-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get $r=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(r-6)$ equal to $0,$ we get $r=6.$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $r=6,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6158975-c81e-5621-aa39-3f2dc728f107" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Manipulating the Equation and Then Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "308cd250-5d9c-5d92-99a8-06286d6838ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520064} {:answer/id #uuid "34f7cfa1-4e93-5517-b155-e270eff09e80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm \\sqrt{3},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520069} {:answer/id #uuid "88dfdb34-3660-5235-afc7-fde23954559d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-2,\\,3,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520193} {:answer/id #uuid "c81ac854-29ab-5769-b7c7-d1a8b87a650d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\sqrt{3},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520269} {:answer/id #uuid "fb90974b-a2c6-5b1d-a585-3e248c3e216d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm 3,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34f7cfa1-4e93-5517-b155-e270eff09e80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm \\sqrt{3},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520069} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea6d0dca-1729-5bc6-9b6f-8503ef6c372f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e7651d9-4306-5281-ab2c-60e5fbcc4dde" :question/math-academy-id "q-114335" :question/problem "Solve $3{t}^{3}-15{t}^{2}-9t+45=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have an overall common factor of $3$, we start by dividing our equation through by $3.$ This gives \n\n$$\n{t}^{3}-5{t}^{2}-3t+15=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3}-5{t}^{2}-3t+15 & = \\\\ ({t}^{3}-5{t}^{2})-(3t-15) & = \\\\ {t}^{2}(t-5)-3(t-5) & = \\\\ (t-5)\\cdot {t}^{2}-(t-5)\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ (t-5)({t}^{2}-3) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve:\n\n- Setting the factor $(t-5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-5 & =0 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({t}^{2}-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-3 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =3 \\\\ t & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions to the given equation are $5$ and $\\pm \\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6158975-c81e-5621-aa39-3f2dc728f107" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Manipulating the Equation and Then Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a4ef76a-ccfb-5791-b25f-9fe6b8c27ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u=\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520052} {:answer/id #uuid "2a4f5de1-9dc9-522b-8d92-8e06bd8036e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u=\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520053} {:answer/id #uuid "3dda4960-6f22-50d0-9a1b-0aa60ac485af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u=-4,\\,\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520079} {:answer/id #uuid "79fdb319-1ee7-52a8-9cfa-8b3ba59ff030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u=\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520167} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b17d87-d9ba-516d-a315-6c82fb45de3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u=-\\frac{3}{4},\\,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a4ef76a-ccfb-5791-b25f-9fe6b8c27ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u=\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520052} :answer-field/id #uuid "888e6ecc-ed2b-57e9-9b31-50cf1eb43d57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4ef63b9-4994-5aab-8c0b-2be94f67268a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114339" :question/problem "Solve $8{u}^{3}-6{u}^{2}-72u+54=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have an overall common factor of $2$, we start by dividing our equation through by $2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2}-36u+27=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2}-36u+27 & = \\\\ (4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2})-(36u-27) & = \\\\ {u}^{2}(4u-3)-9(4u-3) & = \\\\ (4u-3)\\cdot {u}^{2}-(4u-3)\\cdot 9 & = \\\\ (4u-3)({u}^{2}-9) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve:\n\n- Setting the factor $(4u-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-3 & =0 \\\\ 4u & =3 \\\\ u & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({u}^{2}-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2} & =9 \\\\ u & =\\pm 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions to the given equation are $\\frac{3}{4}$ and $\\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6158975-c81e-5621-aa39-3f2dc728f107" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Manipulating the Equation and Then Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45792a27-0fef-5d8f-9ec8-55a9eca333d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520094} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1bc403-f223-53d5-a17e-e48db6c9c1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520308} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9feb0c-7958-5d03-9f8b-fa8015c33036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520311} {:answer/id #uuid "e7778593-47ea-5dd1-bfcc-2dbe06ab0ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520331} {:answer/id #uuid "ecab74bd-d166-5e48-97af-29ff8b13f687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd9feb0c-7958-5d03-9f8b-fa8015c33036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520311} :answer-field/id #uuid "88d0ed58-af5e-5cd7-94e2-e1f54c7e910c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f6abbc6d-e05c-5882-80a0-628ebefcab1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114373" :question/problem "Solve $30{n}^{3}+15{n}^{2}-20n-10=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have an overall common factor of $5$, we start by dividing our equation through by $5.$ This gives \n\n$$\n6{n}^{3}+3{n}^{2}-4n-2=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{n}^{3}+3{n}^{2}-4n-2 & = \\\\ (6{n}^{3}+3{n}^{2})-(4n+2) & = \\\\ 3{n}^{2}(2n+1)-2(2n+1) & = \\\\ (2n+1)\\cdot 3{n}^{2}-(2n+1)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (2n+1)(3{n}^{2}-2) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve:\n\n- Setting the factor $(2n+1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n+1 & =0 \\\\ n & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(3{n}^{2}-2)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{n}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ 3{n}^{2} & =2 \\\\ n & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions to the given equation are $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "385b1ccd-ea68-5c59-a0e6-1a0bb7937460" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations With Leading Coefficients by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1740ebf8-34bc-5bef-9983-7a65b38610cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{4}{3},\\,\\pm \\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520024} {:answer/id #uuid "b88d6d9a-7314-5259-9e8f-d8e3250cd16b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5}{6},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520249} {:answer/id #uuid "bac08756-aaf5-558b-bead-64d9e3ef70b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{6},\\,\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520254} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd8eb40-31a9-59f6-af8c-d8c1138512bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{6},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520277} {:answer/id #uuid "e114765f-9781-5d1d-aec3-c40d54965149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{4}{3},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccd8eb40-31a9-59f6-af8c-d8c1138512bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{6},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520277} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb881c0-119e-5719-8620-d731ed63efa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76829beb-5936-57ec-a144-fda519a19957" :question/math-academy-id "q-14081" :question/problem "Solve $12{y}^{3}+10{y}^{2}-6y-5=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{y}^{3}+10{y}^{2}-6y-5 & = \\\\ (12{y}^{3}+10{y}^{2})-(6y+5) & = \\\\ 2{y}^{2}(6y+5)-(6y+5) & = \\\\ (6y+5)\\cdot 2{y}^{2}-(6y+5)\\cdot 1 & = \\\\ (6y+5)(2{y}^{2}-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(6y+5)(2{y}^{2}-1)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(6y+5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y+5 & =0 \\\\ 6y & =-5 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2{y}^{2}-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ 2{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{5}{6},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6158975-c81e-5621-aa39-3f2dc728f107" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Manipulating the Equation and Then Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068e3f3b-7c3f-5eb4-b735-b11b0f301183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520001} {:answer/id #uuid "142c59d9-de17-5701-9761-3e8d234e26e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{4}{7},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520017} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa263aa-83c7-5421-baaf-8d32501fff76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520168} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e8b378-709c-5af7-a9ce-661162d36425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{8}{5},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520252} {:answer/id #uuid "fd419487-716f-55d1-984d-658897d900d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "068e3f3b-7c3f-5eb4-b735-b11b0f301183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520001} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b7ad001-c3eb-5074-a70e-9b8e370cf6ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "faa06da2-05be-56dd-9e44-883b8d4527f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-14100" :question/problem "Solve $20{y}^{3}+10{y}^{2}-32y-16=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have an overall common factor of $2$, we start by dividing our equation through by $2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n10{y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-16y-8=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-16y-8 & = \\\\ (10{y}^{3}+5{y}^{2})-(16y+8) & = \\\\ 5{y}^{2}(2y+1)-8(2y+1) & = \\\\ (2y+1)\\cdot 5{y}^{2}-(2y+1)\\cdot 8 & = \\\\ (2y+1)(5{y}^{2}-8) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve:\n\n- Setting the factor $(2y+1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y+1 & =0 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(5{y}^{2}-8)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ 5{y}^{2} & =8 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions to the given equation are $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7b17a61-b225-5493-98b0-58d15217aa31" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "119d80a3-bd05-5a7c-b5ae-cdf8a3ef5ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=4,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520014} {:answer/id #uuid "66dd4cf7-8361-590f-810d-636e15e606bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=6,\\,\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520147} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1a9d65-2293-5d5e-9f4e-2c1c6fcac3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=2,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520151} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7a2077-299f-502c-adf4-ae9a95c25adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=2,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520171} {:answer/id #uuid "db1f75da-0620-5683-966e-82579ca015c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=8,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c1a9d65-2293-5d5e-9f4e-2c1c6fcac3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=2,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520151} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1b7f4c0-b2be-59fc-8152-805b6f3979f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f84ff77e-8bf5-5075-9613-766131045ace" :question/math-academy-id "q-14112" :question/problem "Solve ${b}^{3}-2{b}^{2}-6b+12=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{3}-2{b}^{2}-6b+12 & = \\\\ ({b}^{3}-2{b}^{2})-(6b-12) & = \\\\ {b}^{2}(b-2)-6(b-2) & = \\\\ (b-2)\\cdot {b}^{2}-(b-2)\\cdot 6 & = \\\\ (b-2)({b}^{2}-6) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(b-2)({b}^{2}-6)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(b-2)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b-2 & =0 \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({b}^{2}-6)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ {b}^{2} & =6 \\\\ b & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $b=2,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01d58dfd-315a-5a4f-ae16-1db04010169a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations With Negative Leading Coefficients by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116b1441-acff-520b-b6d3-f42fcecb5a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3,\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520013} {:answer/id #uuid "20f7df8b-43e3-5960-bc85-50a52c9e641d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3,\\pm \\frac{1}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520037} {:answer/id #uuid "3e24ec34-1b9f-51ce-9337-9d967ead46f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3,\\pm \\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520081} {:answer/id #uuid "70e32de9-3d4d-5c74-99c2-fe06d0b87974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3,\\pm \\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520155} {:answer/id #uuid "b25a2a64-4e58-5e33-b17b-195d8dc2c1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "116b1441-acff-520b-b6d3-f42fcecb5a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3,\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520013} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b6797a4-3539-5c2b-922f-0342c00d6829" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0e25d3e-3bb1-559e-a9a9-b9db2257d376" :question/math-academy-id "q-37522" :question/problem "Solve $-9{y}^{3}+27{y}^{2}+y-3=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\n9{y}^{3}-27{y}^{2}-y+3=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{3}-27{y}^{2}-y+3 & = \\\\ 9{y}^{2}(y-3)-1(y-3) & = \\\\ (9{y}^{2}-1)(y-3) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(9{y}^{2}-1)(y-3)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(9{y}^{2}-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(y-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=3,\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7b17a61-b225-5493-98b0-58d15217aa31" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Cubic Equations by Grouping"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f294bbf-c65c-5cdd-9fd2-b913ed76bec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520172} {:answer/id #uuid "865b4b4c-4d95-5d8f-897e-8b44bf984a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520188} {:answer/id #uuid "c204a35e-0f2e-5488-b2f7-6ab3e2814650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3,\\,\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520259} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a3fc0a-cc58-5e4b-89f5-8bf18d2b26fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520294} {:answer/id #uuid "ebacee5f-86e2-571f-9218-208ae584000b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5,\\,\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "865b4b4c-4d95-5d8f-897e-8b44bf984a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520188} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e2b231c-9a04-5308-bd1d-78b7f972b284" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e76e6bf7-d54d-5018-81b2-f60c46589b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72088" :question/problem "Solve $y$ if ${y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-2y-10=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-2y-10 & = \\\\ ({y}^{3}+5{y}^{2})-(2y+10) & = \\\\ {y}^{2}(y+5)-2(y+5) & = \\\\ (y+5)\\cdot {y}^{2}-(y+5)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (y+5)({y}^{2}-2) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(y+5)({y}^{2}-2)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(y+5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5 & =0 \\\\ y & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({y}^{2}-2)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-5,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}.$"}]}
